    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d913">

                <pb facs="1204" n="1194" xml:id="pg1194"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24FLC/12–2245</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thomas B. McCabe to
                        Brigadier General Bernhard A. Johnson
                    </hi><anchor n="94" xml:id="d913-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-22">22 December
                        1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>War 89896. In view of State Dept. cable 31 [<hi rendition="#italic">2022</hi>]
                    Dec. 19th,<anchor n="95" xml:id="d913-f2"/> please keep General Marshall<anchor
                        n="96" xml:id="d913-f3"/> fully informed on any conversation being carried
                    on with Chinese concerning Lend-Lease or surplus disposal.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d913-f1" n="94" type="source" xml:id="d913-f1-content">
                <p>Deputy Field Commissioner, China Theater, Office of the Foreign Liquidation
                    Commissioner (OFLC). The OFLC was established in the Department of State in
                    October 1945 with responsibility for the disposition of United States surplus
                    property in foreign areas, Lend-Lease matters, and liberated area
                    requirements.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d913-f2" n="95" xml:id="d913-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Post</hi>, <ref target="#pg1376">p. 1376</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d913-f3" n="96" xml:id="d913-f3-content">
                <p>General of the Army George C. Marshall, Special Representative of President
                    Truman in China.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
